# Commit Message Format

Commitlint enforced. Format: `type(SCOPE): subject`

## Type (required)

`feat`, `fix`, `docs`, `style`, `refactor`, `perf`, `test`, `build`, `ci`, `chore`, `revert`

## Scope (optional)

UPPER-CASE only. Example: `fix(API):`, `feat(V2):`

## Subject (required)

- Present-imperative tense ("add feature" not "added feature")
- No capitalized first letter, no trailing period
- Under 72 characters

## Body/Footer (optional)

- Body: blank line after subject, explain "why" not "what", wrap at 72 chars
- Footer: `Fixes #123`, `Closes #456`, or `BREAKING CHANGE: description`

## Examples

```
fix: correct MySQL mirror numeric comparison for DECIMAL fields
```

```
feat(V2): add batch commit verification for live API tests
```

```
fix: handle DECIMAL precision in MySQL mirror verification

MySQL returns DECIMAL fields with full precision (e.g., 1000.000000)
while expected values may have fewer decimal places. Add numeric
comparison to compare values as numbers when both are valid numbers.
```

```
feat(API): change response format for pagination

BREAKING CHANGE: pagination response now uses 'items' instead of 'data'
```
